    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0176" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.73/136</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Rio de Janeiro</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gottschalk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1144</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 1022 of
                    November 28, 1917,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d67-f1"/> I have the honor to report as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>By decree No. 12,845 of January 17, 1918, published on page 1033 of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Diario Official</hi> (Official Gazette) of January 19,
                    1918, the President of Brazil, in answer to a petition of the Western Telegraph
                    Co., Ltd., alleging the refusal of the Treasury Department to register the
                    contract between this company and the Government (which contract was entered
                    into on December 7, 1917, in virtue of decree No. 12,688 of October 24,
                        1917<anchor n="2" xml:id="d67-f2"/>), has now decreed as follows:</p>
                <p>Clause 22 of decree No. 12,688 shall be amended to read as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The company will enjoy all the advantages granted to similar companies
                            and enterprises excepting the privilege of exemption of customs
                            duties.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. L. M. Gottschalk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
